# WCS Runtime Flows

## Work execution

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant H as Host/API
  participant D as WorkDispatcher
  participant A as Work/Task aggregate
  participant P as Projector
  participant T as TaskDispatcher
  participant G as Agent gateway
  participant U as Agent application
  H->>D: request work creation
  D->>A: create/activate work
  A-->>P: lifecycle event
  A-->>T: task-ready event
  T->>G: assign/dispatch task
  G->>U: task/message
  U->>G: operator/device action
  G->>A: task command
  A-->>P: status event
```

## Agent session

The agent builds configured applications, creates a session, consumes initialization/task/input/equipment/item events, computes display/actions, and routes commands back to TES. Stateful applications update session state after each event.

## Host integration

Importers translate external order/job/work input into core requests. Exporters map selected events to host messages/webhooks. Event monitors run asynchronously.

## Query path

Axon query handlers read projection repositories/caches. They are read models and can lag the event stream when tracking processors are asynchronous.

